 "capsule": "The Han dynasty, founded in 202 BCE when Liu Bang (Emperor Gaozu) defeated his Chu rival Xiang Yu, ruled China for over four centuries and set the enduring template for imperial bureaucracy, Confucian statecraft, and the opening of the Silk Road under Emperor Wu. This span covered the early Rule of Wen and Jing, Emperor Wu's campaigns against the Xiongnu and into Central Asia, and, after the Wang Mang interregnum (9–23 CE), the dynasty's restoration as the Eastern Han from 25 CE. It is entirely distinct from the unrelated medieval Indian Chauhan (Chahamana) dynasty that happens to share its Wikidata identifier.",
